# What is NOT uploaded to EAS Build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Uploads from this machine run at roughly 85 KB/s against a 6.5 MB/s
# download — a badly asymmetric line — and the 5 MB working tree compressed to a 3.4 MB
# tarball that EAS refused three times with `408 Request Timeout`, twice at 100% uploaded.
# The fix is to send less: an Expo build needs `apps/mobile`, `packages/` and the workspace
# manifests, and nothing else here is compiled into an APK or an IPA.
#
# ⚠️  `.easignore` REPLACES `.gitignore` for upload purposes — when this file exists, EAS
# stops consulting `.gitignore` entirely. So everything `.gitignore` excluded has to be
# repeated here, `node_modules/` above all: omitting it would turn a 3.4 MB upload into a
# multi-hundred-megabyte one on the slowest link in the system.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything .gitignore excludes. Keep in step with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
*.bubble
Legacy-Application/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
.secrets.*.env
.DS_Store
dist/
build/
.expo/
*.log
logs/
planning/.backlog-history/
.claude/
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/
# Output of `npm run bundle:check`. Adding this to .gitignore alone was not enough and the
# next upload jumped straight back to 3.4 MB — which is this file's opening warning happening
# in practice, about half an hour after it was written.
.expo-bundle-check/
apps/mobile/.expo-bundle-check/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build the app. This is the part that makes the upload finish.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# THE WEB APP. Not a dependency of the mobile app — and worse than merely unnecessary.
#
# EAS runs `npm ci` at the workspace root, so every dependency of every workspace is installed
# whether the app imports it or not. `apps/web` depends on `sharp`, Astro's image library, which
# is a native module: on 2026-08-14 an iOS build died in "Install dependencies" with
#
#     npm error sharp: Attempting to build from source via node-gyp
#     npm error sharp: Please add node-addon-api to your dependencies
#
# Adding `node-addon-api` would have fixed that build and left the next web-only native package
# to do exactly the same thing. Excluding the workspace is the fix that does not recur: with
# `apps/web` absent the `apps/*` glob resolves to `apps/mobile` alone, `npm ci` stays happy
# because the lockfile's other entries are simply not requested, and neither `sharp` nor `astro`
# is installed at all. Verified by running `npm ci` against a tree with `apps/web` removed.
#
# `packages/` stays: `apps/mobile` genuinely depends on `@graybag/shared`.
#
# `scripts/test/easignore.test.mjs` asserts this line still exists.
apps/web/

# The decision log, specs and learnings: ~1.25 MB of prose the bundler never reads.
docs/

# The menu importer and the image mirror. Node tools that run on a laptop and in CI; they
# are not dependencies of the mobile app.
tools/

# Migrations, pgTAP suites, seed data and Edge Functions. All server-side — Edge Functions
# deploy through `supabase functions deploy`, never through an app build.
supabase/

# Backlog markdown, the generated dashboard and the overnight queue.
planning/

# Repo tooling: backlog sync, migration checks, secret pushing.
scripts/

# CI workflow definitions.
.github/

# `config/` IS NEEDED AND MUST NOT BE EXCLUDED.
#
# It was excluded here at first, on the reasoning that it holds lint configuration the app
# build never runs. That was wrong and cost three builds. `apps/mobile/tsconfig.json` — like
# `packages/shared`'s and `apps/web`'s — begins `"extends": "../../config/tsconfig.base.json"`,
# and Expo's Metro TypeScript resolver follows that chain on startup to read `compilerOptions.
# paths`. With the file absent it throws inside `_loadTsConfigWithExtends`, and the build dies
# in the EAGER_BUNDLE phase with nothing in the CLI output but "Unknown error. See logs of the
# Bundle JavaScript build phase."
#
# It is 28 KB. Excluding it saved nothing and hid the cause behind a generic message.

# The bundle of the pre-rewrite repository, if it is ever copied in here.
*.bundle
